WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.530
- It was important to meet in person

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.280
so there can be no mistake about

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.240
or misrepresentations about
what I wanted to communicate.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.360
I did what I came to do.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.470
- [Interpreter] It was
substantive, it was concrete

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.890
and it took place in an atmosphere

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.360
that was geared towards achieving results.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.760
- American President Joe Biden

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.530
and Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:24.380
have held their first

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.930
much-ballyhooed summit meeting in Geneva.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.750
And what's the story of that summit?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.600
Well, it's really two stories.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.620
The first is a story of the atmospherics

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.590
of their meeting, which
clearly were positive,

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.530
surprisingly so, in fact.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:38.200
The second is the story of the substance

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.130
of their meeting where
it's not at all clear

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.160
that things were quite as positive.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.530
First, the atmospherics.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.030
It was striking how both
leaders emerged describing

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.280
their meeting in positive terms.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.820
President Putin called
President Biden an experienced

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.230
and professional leader

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.350
and even had good words

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.360
to say about the advice Mr. Biden once got

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.400
from his mother.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.730
He said essentially Joe Biden

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.880
is a man of good moral character.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.580
- [Interpreter] It shows the
extent of his moral values.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.721
And that's all quite attractive

00:01:05.721 --> 00:01:10.000
and what I think is on the whole
we spoke the same language.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.980
- [Gerald] That was striking
given that President Biden

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.760
at one point recently said he agreed

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.890
that President Putin
could fairly be described

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.850
as a killer and that he said

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.890
once he didn't see a soul inside him.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:20.820
It also wasn't clear

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.040
how the Putin-Biden personal
relationship might suffer

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.580
in comparison to the admiration
the Russian leader seemed

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.220
to feel for the previous
American president, Donald Trump.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.850
On the Biden side, the US
president said the conversation

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.410
was direct and matter of fact,

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.060
lacking in emotion and he
meant that in a good way,

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.540
and devoice of threats.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.380
He said he succeeded in his main goal,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.240
which was to be sure President Putin knew

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.760
where he was coming from

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.440
when he expressed criticism
of Russian action.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.430
- I told President Putin my
agenda is not against Russia

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.060
or anyone else.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.490
It's for the American people.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.160
- These good atmospherics extended

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.280
to include an agreement

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.390
to return American and Russian ambassadors

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.700
to each other's capitals

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.570
after an absence of several months

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.120
amid rising tensions

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.920
and the two leaders
agreed their governments

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.630
would discussion a prisoner exchange

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.470
that could return some Americans

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.630
that President Biden says

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.160
are being wrongly imprisoned in Russia.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.100
On substance though, the
outcome seemed more mixed.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.190
The two leaders agreed
to set up a working group

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.293
on cyber attacks

00:02:19.293 --> 00:02:22.560
but President Putin defiantly
denied a Russian role

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.360
in cyber attacks and in
recent ransomware cases,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.910
despite ample evidence some of
them do emanate from Russia.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.200
He even suggested more cyber attacks come

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.060
from the US than from Russia,

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.300
raising the question of how
far that working group can get.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.841
- [Interpreter] Most of the
cyber attacks in the world

00:02:38.841 --> 00:02:43.841
are carried out from the cyber
realm of the United States.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.480
In second place is Canada.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.520
Afterwards, Latin American countries

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.110
and then comes Great Britain.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.890
Russia's not on the list.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.330
- [Gerald] Meanwhile, President Biden said

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.420
the Russian leader knows

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.340
the US has considerable cyber power

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.770
of its own and can use it in response

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.500
to further attacks.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.780
The two men agreed to
start a bilateral dialogue

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.540
on strategic stability,

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.201
probably including arms control

00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:08.040
but without a lot of specifics

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.280
and there's a long road to travel there.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.810
President Putin threw
human rights questions back

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.470
at the US by blaming
dissident Alexei Navalny

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.010
for his own arrest.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.730
- [Interpreter] This person knew

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:23.730
that he was breaching the
laws effective in Russia.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.780
He should have noted that has a person

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.520
who was convicted two times.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.790
- [Gerald] And pretending his problems

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:31.750
with political opponents

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.440
at home were somehow comparable

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.880
to the problem the US had

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.450
when a mob attacked the
US Capitol on January 6th.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.900
President Biden, for his part,

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.980
pledged he will continue

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.890
to raise human rights in Russia.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.770
- Human rights is gonna always
be on the table I told him.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:49.290
It's not about just going after Russia

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.170
when they violate human rights,

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.680
it's about who we are.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.190
- [Gerald] There were some
good words about working

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.240
towards similar goals on Afghanistan,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.860
on Iran's nuclear program

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.220
and on humanitarian aid to Syria

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.570
but again, no specifics

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:02.840
and a long ways to go

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.840
to close the gap between
rhetoric and reality.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.890
The bottom line, President
Biden acknowledged

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.030
what is usually the case
with these meetings.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.930
The real concrete results
can't be known immediately

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.600
but will take months or
even years to determine.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.072
- Let's see what happens.

00:04:17.072 --> 00:04:19.680
As that old expression goes,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.710
the proof of the pudding is in the eating.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.003
We're gonna know shortly.

00:04:23.003 --> 00:04:25.670
(pensive music)

